  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\n## What changed\n\nThis PR adds stage 1 of the path kernel (K1, record `## #4024`, \"Stage 1: Region\"). One function builds one region value from a selection, a material side and the bounds. Each guide planner reads this value. The material side is a parameter of its own. No start side reaches the region.\n\nThe old planners do not change. No old planner calls the new code. With the planner switch at its default, all output stays the same. The new region is built beside the old path only in the pins.\n\n### Public surface\n\n- `camcraft_pathkernel::selection::{Chain, Selection}`: `Chain::closed(pts)`, `Chain::open(pts)`, `Selection::new(chains)`, `Selection::face(outer, holes)`, `Selection::points(pts, closed)`. Valid by construction.\n- `camcraft_pathkernel::region(sel, material, bounds, plane, tool, leave) -> Result<KernelRegion, Refusal>` (also `region::region`).\n- `MaterialSide::{Inside, Outside}`: `Inside` cuts the area that the chains enclose; `Outside` cuts the stock round it.\n- `PlanarRegion::new(plane, center, material, part_walls, stock_edge, air, keep_out, tool)`: it now takes the `WorkPlane` and checks the partition and the orientation. New getter `plane()`.\n- Refusal names in `region`: `OPEN_NEEDS_SIDE`, `BAD_LEAVE`, `NEEDS_STOCK`, `OFF_STOCK`, `EMPTY_MATERIAL`, `REGION_GEOMETRY`, `NOT_A_PARTITION`, `NOT_ORIENTED` (and the existing `EMPTY_CENTER`).\n- Refusal names in `selection`: `EMPTY_SELECTION`, `SHORT_CHAIN`, `SELECTION_NOT_FINITE`, `REPEATED_POINT`, `ZERO_AREA`, `SELF_CROSSING`, `CHAINS_CROSS`.\n- The adapter in `camcraft-motion` (`machining2d/kernel_region.rs`, re-exported from `machining2d`): `selection_of_area`, `selection_of_picks`, `contour_material`, `kernel_pocket_selection`, `kernel_bounds_of`, `kernel_pocket_region`.\n\n### Files\n\n- `crates/pathkernel/src/selection.rs` (new), `region_build.rs` (new), `region_check.rs` (new), `region.rs`, `lib.rs`.\n- `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/region.rs` (new submodule of the `laws` directory suite), `laws.rs`, `laws/construction.rs` (the new `PlanarRegion::new` signature; the stock edge is now a loop of the centre).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/kernel_region.rs` and `kernel_region_tests.rs` (new), `mod.rs`.\n- `docs/decisions/4025-kernel-region.md`.\n\n## Pins\n\nKernel (`cargo test -p camcraft-pathkernel --test laws region::`):\n- `the_region_stage_takes_no_start_side` (law 2: the signature).\n- `one_selection_gives_one_region_in_any_pick_order_start_or_direction`.\n- `inside_and_outside_change_only_the_material_side`.\n- `a_region_is_planned_in_the_plane_of_its_recipe_not_in_xy` (the lathe's Z-X plane).\n- `a_keep_out_is_a_part_wall_the_centre_keeps_one_radius_from`.\n- `a_degenerate_selection_is_refused_by_name` (each selection refusal).\n- `a_region_that_cannot_hold_material_is_refused_by_name` (each region refusal).\n- `the_edges_must_partition_the_boundary_of_the_centre`.\n\nMotion (`cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib -- kernel_region`):\n- `one_selection_gives_one_region_through_pocket_contour_and_each_start_side`: the Pocket centre, the Contour Inside centre and the kernel region are one region (symmetric difference below 1e-6 mm2). The pocket carrier gives the same region for Auto, Inside and Outside start sides.\n- `contour_outside_rings_are_the_part_walls_of_the_outside_region`.\n- `the_offset_band_keeps_off_the_stock_edge_and_the_kernel_reaches_it`: a disagreement, pinned (below).\n- `the_pocket_drops_a_sliver_that_contour_and_the_kernel_keep`: a disagreement, pinned (below).\n- `an_open_run_and_an_auto_side_reach_the_kernel_without_a_side`.\n\n## Where two present paths disagree\n\n1. **2D Offset band against Contour Outside, at the stock edge.** The 2D Offset band (`around_part`) erodes the whole band. Its centre stays one tool radius plus the stock to leave inside the stock outline. The kernel's Outside centre reaches the stock outline, as the record's `stock_edge` (\"edges with air beyond them\") reads. The part walls agree within the arc tolerance of the offset (4.8 um; the offset's tolerance is 5 um). Decision 4.\n2. **Pocket against Contour Inside, for a sliver.** The Pocket path drops a centre piece of 0.01 mm2 or less (#2232). Contour Inside keeps it. The kernel keeps the exact erosion; the guide stage's completeness guard decides. Decision 5.\n\n## Decisions\n\nSee `docs/decisions/4025-kernel-region.md` (12 items). The main ones:\n- An open chain is refused by name: it has no inside or outside.\n- `StartSide::around_part` stays on `StartSide`: the old planners read it. The adapter maps it into the region now. The field goes with the old planners.\n- The region holds its `WorkPlane`. The tool is a `ToolShape`, not a radius.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head `e83a31076` (a merge of `origin/side/path-kernel` at `73dc7cb6f`, with #4167 and #4175), Linux, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`:\n- Quick gate, `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: 185 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (48.5 min). The plan has no ui step.\n- `pathkernel suites: laws`: 72 tests pass (the 64 law tests of #4175 and the 8 region tests of this PR).\n- Motion `lib` (with the 5 `kernel_region` pins), `kernel_laws`, and `pass_start_levels` (with the `kernel_baseline` pins of #4165): pass.\n- Example catalog suites by name: `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Earlier head `cfef8048f` (the same region code): `cargo xtask gate light` 6 steps, 0 failed; clippy on `camcraft-app` clean.\n- No heavy step: this is a P2 PR.\n\nThe maintainer decided the Outside-region reading (question dialog, 2026-11-26: \"Yes, to the edge\"). Decision 4 of `docs/decisions/4025-kernel-region.md` records it.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No kind plans through the kernel yet (K6). The adapter is called only by the pins.\n- `ChainSide` and `Containment` of the area controls (open boundaries in `camcraft-app`) are not mapped: the kernel refuses open chains.\n- The `NOT_ORIENTED` guard has no negative test: `camcraft-geometry` gives only normalized regions, so no public value can reach it.\n- No app-level test through `selection_region`: the motion pins compare the present centre functions of the same kinds.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #4025\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
